    "intro_html":  "Real chicken cordon bleu means pounding cutlets flat, rolling them around ham and cheese, breading each one, and praying nothing leaks in the oven. Nobody is doing that fourteen times on a Sunday. This casserole takes the same four flavors, chicken, ham, swiss, and dijon, and layers them in one dish with a cracker topping. Each serving carries 645 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e43 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$1.78 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
